text = "Statistical and Ability Details for the Mage:

- Gain 1d4 Hit Points upon Level-up.

- Access to three chosen Spells from ANY School of Magic.
Influenced by Intelligence.

- Two 1st level Spell Casts at first level, Influenced by Wisdom.

- Proficiency in Reading/Writing.

- THAC0 improves at a rate of 1 every fourth Level.

- The ability to use Scrolls and learn from Spell Tomes.

- No ability to wear armor. Access only to Simple Weapons."

[node name="Wizard Flavor Text" type="Label" parent="."]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
offset_left = 479.0
offset_top = 82.0
offset_right = 1147.0
offset_bottom = 541.0
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_fonts/font = ExtResource("3_su20x")
text = "     The Wizard was born into the Arcane. Raised and annointed with Magic, either through society or 
gifted parents, the Wizard began study at an early age and with great assistance. The Wizard or Witch's 
knowledge goes deeper. They don't have a masterful cantrip. They have a school of Magic within which 
they have been raised. Perhaps it was their mother's specialty or maybe it was their favorite subject in 
school. In any case, they've been steeped in it for years before truly laying their hands on it, but once 
unleashed, they're unmatched.
     The Wizard comes equipped with a Grimoire. The Grimoire is a personalized hand-crafted spellbook 
assosciated with any one School of Magic: Illusion, Enchantment/Charm, Conjuration, Abjuration, 
Necromancy, Invocation/Evocation, Divination, or Alteration. The Grimoire shares an affinity for 
this School and all spells of its type are enhanced in some way. This affinity, and related schooling, means
that every available Spell of the specialized School must be taken before other Spells at that Spell Level
are allowed; and the School opposite of the chosen School may never be taken.
     The Wizard/Witch knew they were destined for a life of peril and took lessons in swordplay, swords 
being an optimal implement amongst weapons for channelling Magic. This makes Wizards a compelling 
fighter in addition to wielding the Arcane Art and attacks can be attempted in addition to the casting of 
a Spell within the same round. The sudden footwork of being engaged in melee is not conducive to the
ridgidity typically required to weave a Spell, but the long hours of childhood study provide the familiarity
required. It is marginally less subtle than the flick of a wrist, however. Integral to the impressive ability
to strike with a weapon and simultaneously cast a Spell is the Grimoire. The Witch or Wizard has 
wielded the Arcane through this tome their entire lives and should a Grimoire be lost, so to is this 
formidable talent."

